INT. CALL CENTER IN A FORMER CHURCH - DAY

Cubicles fill the nave. Gothic arches overhead, fluorescent panels bolted to the vaulted ceiling. Where the altar stood, a standing desk with a headset-wearing mannequin. Stained glass casts blue and amber light on rows of identical monitors. A hand-lettered banner above the apse reads: "YOUR CALL IS A BLESSING."

At a long table once used for communion, DESMOND PEMBERTON-AGYEMAN (40s, gray suit, lanyard) stands holding a cardboard box of personal effects. Across from him sits LAVINIA OKORO-HALVERSEN (50s, floral blouse, reading glasses pushed up on her head), the floor manager, a clipboard in her lap.

LAVINIA
Desmond. Sit.

DESMOND
I'd rather stand, Lavinia.

LAVINIA
It's not a sermon.

DESMOND
It feels like one.

She pats the pew-bench beside her. He doesn't move. A phone rings somewhere in the nave and is picked up on the second ring.

LAVINIA
Fourteen years, Desmond.

DESMOND
Fifteen in March.

LAVINIA
Fifteen. Well, you've done admirable work.

DESMOND
Is this the part where you tell me why I'm leaving?

LAVINIA
It isn't a leaving. It's a reallocation.

DESMOND
Of what?

LAVINIA
Of you.

DESMOND
To where?

LAVINIA
Upstairs.

DESMOND
We have an upstairs?

LAVINIA
The bell tower.

He looks up. Far overhead, a narrow staircase vanishes into the rafters. Dust turns in a shaft of colored light.

DESMOND
What's in the bell tower?

LAVINIA
The new quality-assurance team.

DESMOND
How many on it?

LAVINIA
One.

DESMOND
Who?

LAVINIA
You.

Desmond sets the box on the table. Rummages in it, finds a mug that reads "WORLD'S OKAYEST AGENT," holds it for a long moment, and places it carefully on the desk.

DESMOND
(to the nave)
Everyone. A moment, please.

The call center falls silent. Forty heads in forty cubicles rise above forty partitions.

DESMOND (CONT'D)
(to the room)
I'm being promoted to the bell tower.

Silence. Somewhere, a headset clatters to the floor. Somewhere in the back, someone begins to clap, stops, and thinks better of it.

LAVINIA
(low, to Desmond)
Please don't make a scene.

DESMOND
(low, to Lavinia)
I'm only making an announcement.

LAVINIA
That's how scenes begin.

He lifts the box. Turns toward the staircase. Pauses at the foot of it, one hand on the rail.

DESMOND
(to himself)
Fifteen years. Finally, a view.

He climbs. The stairs creak. Lavinia lowers the clipboard onto the communion table and gazes up after him, her face unreadable in the colored light.

LAVINIA
(quietly, to no one)
Do you know, I think he'll do very well up there.

A bell rings, once, from high above. All forty headsets chime at the same instant: "Thank you for calling. Your call is a blessing."
